        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0099" n="67" xml:id="pg67"/>

                <head>35. Memorandum From the Joint Chiefs of Staff to Secretary of Defense
                        McNamara<anchor n="0" xml:id="d35-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">JCSM-57-61</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-02-03">February 3,
                        1961</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Military Evaluation of the Cuban Plan</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached hereto is the Military Evaluation of the Central Intelligence Agency
                    Para-Military Plan, Cuba. Subject to your concurrence,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d35-f2"/> the Joint Chiefs of Staff propose to forward copies of
                    their assessment of the plan to the Director for Central Intelligence with the
                    proposal that they meet with the Director for Central Intelligence and members
                    of his staff for further discussion of this project.</p>
                <closer><signed>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff:<lb/><hi rendition="#bold">L.L.
                            Lemnitzer</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d35-f3"/><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chairman<lb/>Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff</hi></signed></closer>





                <xi:include href="d35-a1.xml" xpointer="d35-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d35-a2.xml" xpointer="d35-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d35-a3.xml" xpointer="d35-a3"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d35-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d35-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, Cuba,
                    Subjects, Taylor Report. Top Secret; Limited Distribution. According to a May 4
                    memorandum in which he detailed his briefings of the JCS on the paramilitary
                    plan, Major General David W. Gray gave the JCS a 20-minute briefing on February
                    3 on the CIA Para-Military Plan, Trinidad area, which is outlined in JCSM-57-61.
                    (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d35-f2" n="1" xml:id="d35-f2-content">
                <p>In a handwritten note on the source text at this point, McNamara authorized the
                    Joint Chiefs to forward the assessment to the CIA and to discuss the project
                    with CIA officials in light of the assessment.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d35-f3" n="2" xml:id="d35-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that indicates Lemnitzer signed the original.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
